+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+`add`, `rename` and `tag` in `src/domain/list.ts` accept any string. The domain must not throw and must return a `Result` (project rules), and must not read the clock or randomness.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+- One place that defines validity; clear messages; no state change on rejection.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+- Validating titles in `find`/`get`/`complete`/`untag` lookups.
+- Rejecting duplicate titles differently (still `duplicate`).
+
+## Decisions
+
+- New pure module `src/domain/validate.ts` with `validateTitle`, `validatePriority`, `validateTag` returning `Result<string>`, plus `MAX_TITLE_LENGTH = 120`. The list calls them before touching any state, so a failure returns early.
+- Add error code `invalid-input` to `TodoErrorCode`, rather than reusing `invalid-state`, so programs can tell it apart.
+- Title length is measured after trimming, consistent with titles being stored trimmed.
+- Validation runs before lookup in `rename`/`tag`, so invalid input is reported even for an unknown task.
+- `add` validates all of title, priority and tags before consuming an id, so ids are not skipped on rejection. Tags passed to `add` are validated too.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Existing callers that relied on odd input now get errors; this is the intent.
+- Tags are not trimmed: `" a"` contains a space and is rejected.
