+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Some screens pass whatever the user typed straight to the list, so odd tasks get in: blank or huge titles, unknown priorities, empty or spaced tags. The list should refuse them with a clear error.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Adding, renaming or tagging a task validates its input and returns an `invalid-input` error saying what is wrong.
+- Rejected: a title empty or only spaces; a title over 120 characters; a priority other than `low`, `normal`, `high`; a tag that is empty or contains a space.
+- A rejected call changes nothing in the list (no task added, renamed or tagged, no `updatedAt` change).
+- New error code `invalid-input` in `TodoErrorCode`.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `input-validation`: which task titles, priorities and tags the list accepts, and the error when it rejects one.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/domain/result.ts` (new error code), new `src/domain/validate.ts`, `src/domain/list.ts` (`add`, `rename`, `tag`), `test/list.test.ts`, `README.md`.
+- No new dependency.
